 About ACE

 At ACE, you will join a forward-looking consulting and RegTech firm in the financial heart of Amsterdam. We are specialised in regulatory change, risk & data, AI, financial & non-financial risk, and sustainable finance within the financial services sector. Together we future-proof regulatory change by combining strong human connections with innovative technology like our GenAI-enabled workbench RegAI. You will support financial institutions in their regulatory change management challenges enabled by our own AI solutions.

At ACE, you will be part of more than just a niche consulting and RegTech firm. You will join an inclusive community where you can be yourself, learn and grow, and thrive. Our culture is built on authentic connections, mutual commitments, a shared passion for impact, and bold leadership.

Working at ACE means being part of an ambitious, dynamic, and results-driven team that also knows how to have fun. You will collaborate with colleagues from over 10 different nationalities, where every member is a trusted adviser and valued for their uniqueness. With our hybrid workplace model, you balance high performance with personal well-being.

 About You

 You have a strong affinity with responsible AI and are up to date on the newest (AI)technologies, emerging AI regulatory requirements and AI Ethics. You have the skills to support clients in navigating the dynamic AI landscape, by enabling them to successfully implement their AI strategy in a responsible way. This means adopting a solid AI governance structure and having a strong change capacity. You can combine being practical with your expertise to empower clients being successful in adopting responsible AI practices while ensuring compliance. While you may not be an expert in implementing AI practices just yet, your solid background in project management within the financial services sector positions you perfectly to embrace this challenge. You can work independently, engage effectively with stakeholders, and manage projects from inception to completion. When facing challenges, you can identify issues and seek assistance to ensure project success and client satisfaction. What is crucial is your readiness to learn and lead in this evolving field. If you have experience in managing projects and a passion for AI’s transformative potential, we encourage you to apply.

What will you do

You will help our clients harness the value of AI to drive better business outcomes by guiding them in adopting AI technologies responsibly. You will orchestrate the required changes in our clients’ organisation that will bolster a successful implementation of the AI strategy and support the organisation with your expertise. As a (senior) manager, you are guiding junior professionals in mastering the art of responsible AI navigation. Together, you will work towards a future where technology powers finance in a way that is fair, transparent and secure.

 Role

 In this multifaceted role, you will undertake tasks that blend strategic leadership with hands-on project management, while fostering client relationships. Your main activities will include:

 Strategic leadership & vision: Guide financial institutions in crafting and applying responsible AI (governance) strategies. Your ability to envision how AI can be responsibly utilized within the financial sector—balancing innovation with ethical considerations and compliance—is key. While direct experience in AI governance is a plus, what is crucial is your strategic mindset and project management skills.
 Client engagement: Act as a trusted advisor to clients, illuminating the path to responsible AI adoption. Your skills in understanding client needs and articulating the value of responsible AI will help in engaging both prospective and existing clients.
 Project management: Lead projects that embed AI into operations responsibly. This includes everything from policy advisory to ensuring regulatory compliance. Your project management experience, also outside of AI-specific contexts, will be invaluable as you steer these initiatives to success.
 Innovation and thought leadership: Stay at the forefront of AI technology trends and ethical practices. A commitment to continuous learning will enable you to assess new developments and advise clients effectively, ensuring our firm remains a thought leader in responsible AI.


 Experience you will bring

 At least 5 years of experience in consultancy within the financial sector;
 Demonstrated affinity with AI, responsible AI practices, or related fields, underpinned by an understanding of AI technologies and their implications;
 A Master’s degree in a relevant field such as Business, Economics, Technology, or Data Science;
 A track record of leading transformation projects from conception through to implementation that reflect commitment to authenticity, impact, and quality;
 Familiarity with regulatory frameworks and standards related to AI ethics, privacy, and data protection;
 Proven ability in leading teams and mentoring juniors;
 Excellent communication and presenting skills in English;
 You have an existing network in the domain, you are able to nurture client relationships, bring our propositions to the client, and recognise new commercial opportunities to help ACE grow.


 What we offer

We are an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. Joining ACE means becoming part of a culture that values you as an individual, prioritizes your work/life balance, and encourages continuous learning and development. With the right balance, we believe you’ll feel happier and more committed to your personal and professional growth, which is an important focus area within our firm. In addition to a salary that is based on education, expertise, experience and performance, benefits

 You Can Expect Include

 Profit-sharing scheme;
 Non-contributory pension scheme;
 Flexible mobility allowance;
 28 paid holidays;
 Sharing company value with virtual shares;
 Comprehensive on-the-job training to enhance your professional growth;
 Tailored trainings to elevate your skills;
 Personal development budget for your learning and growth;
 A commitment to the ‘Great Place to Work’ initiative, meaning you will work in an environment that nurtures your well-being and values inclusivity, ensuring you thrive;
 Working for a company with an EcoVadis Gold certification, showcasing our dedication to sustainability and ethical operations;
 Voluntary social -and leisure activities, featuring ‘Funky Fridays’ and an annual office trip.


 Ready to make an impact?

If you are eager to join a firm where you can truly be yourself, leading with courage, innovation, and a deep commitment to making a positive impact, and if you’re ready to drive innovation in regulatory technology and make tangible impact on the financial ssector, we want to hear from you. So dive right in and apply today!

To apply or if you have any questions, reach out to us with you CV and motivation letter via email info@acecompany.nl












